Will you be using a conduction velocity vector in the left atrial appendage to simulate fiber direction?
Note: If you enable this option, make sure the model you are running includes a mapped left atrial appendage (LAA). 
This vector will be used to determine the direction of maximum conduction velocity.
The first variable is a Boolean that indicates whether this feature is enabled.
The second variable is a float that specifies the reduction factor for a muscle running perpendicular to this vector. 
All other muscles will have their conduction velocities scaled between 1.0 and this value, depending on the angle 
between the muscle and the vector.
--UseLAApendageVelocityScaling ~ ###
--MaxLAApendageVelocityReduction ~ ###

Will you be using a conduction velocity vector in the left atrial body to simulate fiber direction?
This vector will be used to determine the direction of maximum conduction velocity.
The first variable is a Boolean that indicates whether this feature is enabled.
The second variable is an integer that specifies the model type:
1: Flat sheet
2: Sphere
3: Idealized model or anatomically accurate model generated from CT scans
If you select model type 3, make sure the model has its pulmonary veins mapped.
The third variable is a float that specifies the reduction factor for a muscle running perpendicular to this vector. 
All other muscles will have their conduction velocities scaled between 1.0 and this value, 
depending on the angle between the muscle and the vector.
--UseLABodyVelocityScaling ~ ###
--LABodyType ~ ###
--MaxLABodyVelocityReduction ~ ###

Connection line width for the lines that represent muscles connecting the nodes:
1.0 to 3.0 works well for simulations with many nodes, and 5.0 to 10.0 is suitable for simulations with fewer nodes.
It should be a float.
	
--LineWidth = 1.0;

Set the size of the node spheres here. It is scaled by the RadiusOfLeftAtrium. A good value is 0.01.
It should be a float.

--NodeRadiusAdjustment = 0.005;

Set the size of a point drawn if shperes are turned off but you still want to see the node. A good value is 5.0 to 10.0.
It should be a float.

--NodePointSize = 1.5;

Background color (Background of the scene): red, green, blue.
